---
import { statSync } from "node:fs";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

// the setup app is built by PyInstaller from tools/setup/neem_setup.py
const size = (statSync("public/download/neem-setup.exe").size / 1e6).toFixed(1);
---

<Base
  title="Download"
  description="Neem for Windows: one setup app installs Neem on your computer and opens the heat maps, the planner and the physics API in your browser."
  path="/download"
  night
>
  <section class="wrap head page-head">
    <p class="kicker">Download</p>
    <h1 class="display dl-title">Neem for Windows.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      One file sets Neem up on your computer and opens it in your browser: the heat maps, the
      planner and the physics API, all running on your own machine.
    </p>
    <p class="dl-get">
      <a class="button" href="/download/neem-setup.exe" download>Download neem-setup.exe</a>
      <span class="small muted">{size} MB · Windows 10 or 11</span>
    </p>
  </section>

  <article class="wrap body">
    <section class="block rule">
      <h2 class="title">What it does</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <ol class="steps">
          <li>Installs <b>uv</b> and <b>Bun</b> if you don't have them, each from its official installer.</li>
          <li>Downloads Neem's code from GitHub into <code>%LOCALAPPDATA%\Neem</code>.</li>
          <li>Installs the Python and web packages. The first run takes a few minutes and about 2 GB.</li>
          <li>Starts the physics API and the site, and opens Neem in your browser.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>
          Run it again any time to start Neem; it skips what is already there. Close its window to
          stop Neem.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="block rule">
      <h2 class="title">If Windows asks</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          The app isn't code-signed yet, so Windows SmartScreen may say it comes from an unknown
          publisher. Choose <b>More info</b>, then <b>Run anyway</b>. Nothing in it is hidden: its
          source is <code>tools/setup/neem_setup.py</code> in the repository, about 150 lines of
          plain Python, built into one file with PyInstaller.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="block rule">
      <h2 class="title">What you need</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Windows 10 or 11, an internet connection for the first run, and about 2 GB of disk. A
          graphics card makes SOLWEIG faster; without one it runs on the processor. The planner's
          agent needs <a href="https://ollama.com">Ollama</a> with <code>qwen3:4b</code>, and building
          twins of new schools needs the open-data pipeline; the <a href="/docs#run">docs</a> walk
          through both.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="block rule">
      <h2 class="title">Mac or Linux</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Three commands do the same by hand, with <code>uv</code> and <code>bun</code> installed:
        </p>
        <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/riteshroshann/neem && cd neem
uv sync && uv run neem-api        # the physics API on :8000
cd web && bun install && bun run dev   # the site on :4321</code></pre>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .head {
    padding-bottom: var(--s-8);
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--s-6);
  }

  .dl-title {
    max-width: 10ch;
  }

  .dl-get {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--s-4) var(--s-5);
  }

  .body {
    padding-bottom: var(--section);
  }

  .block {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 340px) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: var(--s-8);
    padding-block: var(--s-7) var(--s-8);
  }

  .steps {
    margin: 0 0 var(--s-4);
    padding-left: 1.2em;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--s-2);
  }

  pre {
    margin: var(--s-4) 0 0;
    padding: var(--s-4) var(--s-5);
    overflow-x: auto;
    font: 500 var(--t-s) / 1.7 var(--sans);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  code {
    font: 500 0.95em var(--sans);
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .block {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: var(--s-5);
    }
  }
</style>
